  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This page covers 8(a) Business Development set-aside federal contracts for FY2026 to date. Total obligations are $6.2B across 8,204 awards, with an average award size of $750K. Obligations are down 55.0% year over year, and current-year totals are partial since the fiscal year is ongoing. The Department of Defense accounts for the largest share of FY2026 to date obligations at $3.1B. Other top buying agencies include the Department of Health and Human Services at $549M and the Department of Homeland Security at $522M. The biggest individual 8(a) contractors so far are AKIMA FACILITIES OPERATIONS LLC at $85.5M and CHEROKEE NATION STRATEGIC PROGRAMS, L.L.C. at $73M. Leading industries by obligations include Computer Systems Design Services at $745M and Other Computer Related Services at $633M. Readers should note the data are contract obligations and represent fiscal year to date totals that will change as FY2026 progresses.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are FY2026 8(a) obligations by agency?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, with $3.1B in obligations. The next two agencies by obligations are the Department of Health and Human Services at $549M and the Department of Homeland Security at $522M. Together those three agencies account for a substantial portion of the $6.2B reported for FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors lead FY2026 8(a) activity?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services leads industries with $745M in obligations, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $633M and Facilities Support Services at $624M. The top vendors are AKIMA FACILITIES OPERATIONS LLC at $85.5M and CHEROKEE NATION STRATEGIC PROGRAMS, L.L.C. at $73M, followed by ASRC FEDERAL TECHNOLOGY SOLUTIONS, LLC at $64.5M, SYNERGY BUSINESS INNOVATION & SOLUTIONS INC. at $49.2M, JBW GROUP LLC at $49M, and AGILE DECISION SCIENCES, LLC at $46M."
      }
    ]
  },
